EQUIVALENT FX-CMP-012  -- proved, not searched for: in the choice of the latest stored rate `f[fx_date] > best[date]` becomes `>=`.  The two differ only when two usable rates for the same pair carry the same date.  The natural key of an fx_rate record is exactly `<fx_date>|<pair>` (ingest_templates/TPL-BZ-FX-RATES.json natural_key [fx_date, pair]; both fields are read from the same two columns), so the same pair and date is the same key: a second delivery is a revision or a conflict (a conflict is skipped before this line), never a second usable record.  Non-canonical dates are refused at intake (INVALID_DATE) and a differently written pair is a different pair that the pair test skips.  Pinned by test_mkt_edges_base (a stored rate is keyed by its own day and pair, so two never tie).
