EQUIVALENT LD-CMP-040  -- proved, not searched for: the sort key of the landed sources `(s[0], s[1] if s[1] is not None else -1)` becomes `... is None ...`.  Python compares the second element of two key tuples only when their first elements are equal, and every source is a (record reference, pinned revision) pair where F.rev gives one revision per reference for the whole run (apg/fin/snap.py Facts.rev reads the pins), the list is a set, and each tier, term and assumption is listed once.  So no two sources share a reference and the second element never decides the order.  Pinned by test_mkt_edges_landed (a source reference appears once per landed record).
