EQUIVALENT LD-CMP-042  -- proved, not searched for: in landed.purchase_plan the note test `alt[buy_qty_micro] > need_micro` becomes `>=`.  An alternative exists only when its tier start t[0] is strictly above base[buy_qty_micro] (the guard on the line above, whose mutant LD-CMP-008 is killed), the alternative buys at least t[0], and base[buy_qty_micro] = max(need, minimum order) rounded up to a pack size, which is at least need.  So alt buy > t[0]-1 >= base buy >= need: strictly greater, and `>=` gives the same answer.  Pinned by test_mkt_edges_landed (a larger tier always buys strictly more than the need).
