EQUIVALENT RU-BOL-028  -- proved, not searched for: in rules MP06 the condition for writing an fx_observed event `ref_conv[status] == converted and ref_conv[rate_source_ref]` becomes `or`.  MP06 skips home-currency quotes before this line, so fx.convert takes its foreign-currency path, where a found rate returns status converted with rate_source_ref = fx_rate/<key> (never empty) and a missing rate returns not_converted with rate_source_ref None.  The two operands are therefore always both true or both false (the only status/source split, none_same_currency, is unreachable here), and `and` and `or` give the same answer.  Pinned by test_mkt_edges_rules (a foreign conversion is converted with a source, or not converted with none).
